@title 911 Call Receiving and Dispatch
@subtitle Architecture for the Marrow County Emergency Communications District
@author Public Safety Systems team
@date 2026-09-30

## Overview
Calls arrive from the telephone carriers into the primary dispatch center. A backup dispatch center across the county can take over if the primary is lost.

## Call path
diagram callpath dir=LR title="Call path"
callpath: callers "Callers" ext
callpath: carriers "Telecom Carriers" ext
callpath: router "Call Router" svc
callpath: cada "CAD Server A" svc "active" focus
callpath: cadb "CAD Server B" svc "hot standby"
callpath: radio "Radio Gateway" svc
callpath: sbr "Standby Call Router" svc
callpath: repl "CAD Replica" store
callpath: gis "State GIS Service" ext
callpath: field "Field Units" user
callpath: callers -> carriers : voice and caller location
callpath: carriers -> router : SIP trunks
callpath: router -> cada : call record
callpath: cada -> cadb : state sync
callpath: cada --> repl : asynchronous replication
callpath: router --> sbr : heartbeat
callpath: cada -> gis : address lookup
callpath: cada -> radio : dispatch message
callpath: radio -> field : P25 radio
callpath: group pdc "Primary Dispatch Center" router, cada, cadb, radio
callpath: group bdc "Backup Dispatch Center" sbr, repl

!! The backup center is activated only when the shift supervisor declares the primary unavailable. It is never activated automatically.

## Failover targets
- Call routing switches to the Standby Call Router within 30 seconds.
- CAD Server B takes over within 2 minutes.
- The CAD Replica lags by under 5 seconds.
- The whole backup center is fully staffed and taking calls within 10 minutes.
